      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xloader__server__apis_1ga9870c3bf75d6cfbd669c535dd7f7a589" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XLoader_CalibDataRestore</definition>
        <argsstring>(XPlmi_Cmd *Cmd)</argsstring>
        <name>XLoader_CalibDataRestore</name>
        <param>
          <type>XPlmi_Cmd *</type>
          <declname>Cmd</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function restores the calibration data of the warm-boot DDR memory controllers carried in the command. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The storage device is the primary boot device. JTAG, SMAP/SBI, PCIe and SD/eMMC raw boot skip the restore and return success. A fetch or integrity failure for one DDR MC clears its calibration skip flag so that MC cold-calibrates, and the command continues.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>Cmd</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>is pointer to the command structure. Cmd-&gt;Len is the full payload, one pair per warm-boot DDR MC, and may be empty when no DDR MC requested warm boot:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Physical address of the DDR MC.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Storage offset. For QSPI/OSPI this is the flash address of the record. A CDO chunk can deliver fewer words than Cmd-&gt;Len. That chunk is accepted, and the restore runs only on the chunk that finishes the command.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS on success.</para></listitem><listitem><para>Error Code in case of failure </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
